{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-40577" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following statements is true regarding the series  ${\\sum }_{n=3}^{\\infty }\\frac{2}{15}{(\\frac{6}{5})}^{n-1}$ ?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061011/state.json" "file_sha256" "1302063638b0492d24f629b222a7668b63f521604190ad74036b4fa646a50d20"} {"question" "q-40577" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The series starts with $n=3.$ So the common ratio is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\frac{{a}_{4}}{{a}_{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{2}{15}{(\\frac{6}{5})}^{4-1}}{\\frac{2}{15}{(\\frac{6}{5})}^{3-1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{(\\frac{6}{5})}^{3}}{{(\\frac{6}{5})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the series is divergent because $|r|\\ge 1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061011/state.json" "file_sha256" "1302063638b0492d24f629b222a7668b63f521604190ad74036b4fa646a50d20"} {"question" "q-40577" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061011/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1f7e751085fd07f1489c3a19d30da6ecca0a3a79dc9e1d04394688174adb53b1"} {"question" "q-40577" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061011/state.json" "file_sha256" "1302063638b0492d24f629b222a7668b63f521604190ad74036b4fa646a50d20"} {"question" "q-40577" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "Inconclusive because $|r|=1$"] ["text" "The series is convergent because $|r|<1$"] ["text" "The series is convergent because $|r|\\ge 1$"] ["text" "The series is divergent because $|r|<1$"] ["text" "The series is divergent because $|r|\\ge 1$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061011/state.json" "file_sha256" "1302063638b0492d24f629b222a7668b63f521604190ad74036b4fa646a50d20"} {"question" "q-40577" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "The series is divergent because $|r|\\ge 1$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061011/state.json" "file_sha256" "1302063638b0492d24f629b222a7668b63f521604190ad74036b4fa646a50d20"} {"question" "q-50607" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For which values of $k$ does the series ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{{3}^{kn-2}}{{9}^{n-1}}$ converge?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061011/state.json" "file_sha256" "1302063638b0492d24f629b222a7668b63f521604190ad74036b4fa646a50d20"} {"question" "q-50607" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rewrite the series so that it's in the form ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }a{r}^{n},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{{3}^{kn-2}}{{9}^{n-1}} & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{{3}^{kn}\\cdot {3}^{-2}}{{9}^{n-1}} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{9}(\\frac{{3}^{kn}}{{9}^{n-1}}) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }(\\frac{{3}^{kn}}{{9}^{n}}) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{(\\frac{{3}^{k}}{9})}^{n}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that this is a geometric series with a common ratio of $r=\\frac{{3}^{k}}{9}.$ \n\nFor the series to converge, we require $|r|<1.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\frac{{3}^{k}}{9}| & <1 \\\\ \\frac{{3}^{k}}{9} & <1 \\\\ {3}^{k} & <9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we could remove the absolute value bars because $\\frac{{3}^{k}}{9}$ is always positive.\n\nThe equation ${3}^{k}=9$ has the solution $k=2.$ Now, since ${3}^{k}$ increases as $k$ increases, the solution to ${3}^{k}<9$ must be $k<2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061011/state.json" "file_sha256" "1302063638b0492d24f629b222a7668b63f521604190ad74036b4fa646a50d20"} {"question" "q-50607" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061011/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1f7e751085fd07f1489c3a19d30da6ecca0a3a79dc9e1d04394688174adb53b1"} {"question" "q-50607" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061011/state.json" "file_sha256" "1302063638b0492d24f629b222a7668b63f521604190ad74036b4fa646a50d20"} {"question" "q-50607" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "k<1"] ["math" "k<2"] ["math" "k<4"] ["math" "k>2"] ["math" "k>4"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061011/state.json" "file_sha256" "1302063638b0492d24f629b222a7668b63f521604190ad74036b4fa646a50d20"} {"question" "q-50607" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "k<2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061011/state.json" "file_sha256" "1302063638b0492d24f629b222a7668b63f521604190ad74036b4fa646a50d20"} {"question" "q-124898" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following statements is true regarding the series  ${\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }(-2){(-0.75)}^{n}$ ?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061011/state.json" "file_sha256" "1302063638b0492d24f629b222a7668b63f521604190ad74036b4fa646a50d20"} {"question" "q-124898" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The series starts with $n=0.$ So the common ratio is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\frac{{a}_{1}}{{a}_{0}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-2){(-0.75)}^{1}}{(-2){(-0.75)}^{0}} \\\\  & =-0.75.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the series is convergent because $|r|<1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061011/state.json" "file_sha256" "1302063638b0492d24f629b222a7668b63f521604190ad74036b4fa646a50d20"} {"question" "q-124898" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061011/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1f7e751085fd07f1489c3a19d30da6ecca0a3a79dc9e1d04394688174adb53b1"} {"question" "q-124898" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061011/state.json" "file_sha256" "1302063638b0492d24f629b222a7668b63f521604190ad74036b4fa646a50d20"} {"question" "q-124898" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "Inconclusive because $|r|=1.$"] ["text" "The series is convergent because $|r|<1.$"] ["text" "The series is convergent because $|r|\\ge 1.$"] ["text" "The series is divergent because $|r|<1.$"] ["text" "The series is divergent because $|r|\\ge 1.$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061011/state.json" "file_sha256" "1302063638b0492d24f629b222a7668b63f521604190ad74036b4fa646a50d20"} {"question" "q-124898" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "The series is convergent because $|r|<1.$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061011/state.json" "file_sha256" "1302063638b0492d24f629b222a7668b63f521604190ad74036b4fa646a50d20"} {"question" "q-124913" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following geometric series converge?\n\n- $162+108+72+48+⋯$\n- $1-\\frac{3}{4}+\\frac{9}{16}-\\frac{27}{64}+⋯$\n- $-10-9-8.1-7.29-⋯$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061011/state.json" "file_sha256" "1302063638b0492d24f629b222a7668b63f521604190ad74036b4fa646a50d20"} {"question" "q-124913" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's look at each series in turn.\n\n- For the geometric series $162+108+72+48+⋯$ the common ratio is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}} & =\\frac{108}{162} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the series is convergent because $|r|<1.$\n\n- For the geometric series $1-\\frac{3}{4}+\\frac{9}{16}-\\frac{27}{64}+⋯$ the common ratio is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}} & =\\frac{(-\\frac{3}{4})}{1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the series is convergent because $|r|<1.$\n\n- For the geometric series $-10-9-8.1-7.29-⋯$  the common ratio is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}} & =\\frac{-9}{-10} \\\\  & =0.9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the series is convergent because $|r|<1.$\n\nIn conclusion, series I, II, and III converge." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061011/state.json" "file_sha256" "1302063638b0492d24f629b222a7668b63f521604190ad74036b4fa646a50d20"} {"question" "q-124913" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061011/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1f7e751085fd07f1489c3a19d30da6ecca0a3a79dc9e1d04394688174adb53b1"} {"question" "q-124913" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061011/state.json" "file_sha256" "1302063638b0492d24f629b222a7668b63f521604190ad74036b4fa646a50d20"} {"question" "q-124913" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I, II, and III"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061011/state.json" "file_sha256" "1302063638b0492d24f629b222a7668b63f521604190ad74036b4fa646a50d20"} {"question" "q-124913" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I, II, and III"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061011/state.json" "file_sha256" "1302063638b0492d24f629b222a7668b63f521604190ad74036b4fa646a50d20"} {"question" "q-351365" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the range of values of $k$ for which the series\n${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{(\\frac{9}{{81}^{k}})}^{n}$\nconverges. Do not round the answer.\n\n$k$\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061011/state.json" "file_sha256" "1302063638b0492d24f629b222a7668b63f521604190ad74036b4fa646a50d20"} {"question" "q-351365" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We see that this is a geometric series with a common ratio of $r=\\frac{9}{{81}^{k}}.$\n\nFor the series to converge, we require $|r|<1.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\frac{9}{{81}^{k}}| & <1 \\\\ \\frac{9}{{81}^{k}} & <1 \\\\ 9 & <{81}^{k} \\\\ {81}^{k} & >9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we could remove the absolute value bars because $\\frac{9}{{81}^{k}}$ is always positive.\n\nThe equation ${81}^{k}=9$ has the solution $k=\\frac{1}{2}.$ Now, since ${81}^{k}$ increases as $k$ increases, the solution to ${81}^{k}>9$ must be $k>\\frac{1}{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061011/state.json" "file_sha256" "1302063638b0492d24f629b222a7668b63f521604190ad74036b4fa646a50d20"} {"question" "q-351365" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061011/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1f7e751085fd07f1489c3a19d30da6ecca0a3a79dc9e1d04394688174adb53b1"} {"question" "q-351365" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061011/state.json" "file_sha256" "1302063638b0492d24f629b222a7668b63f521604190ad74036b4fa646a50d20"} {"question" "q-351365" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math ">"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061011/state.json" "file_sha256" "1302063638b0492d24f629b222a7668b63f521604190ad74036b4fa646a50d20"} {"question" "q-351365" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061011/state.json" "file_sha256" "1302063638b0492d24f629b222a7668b63f521604190ad74036b4fa646a50d20"} {"question" "q-351365" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061011/state.json" "file_sha256" "1302063638b0492d24f629b222a7668b63f521604190ad74036b4fa646a50d20"}] "usage" {} "basis" 1948 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
